Fix: the view space light positions are reused after the view changed, so objects are lit from wrong light positions.

Description
  OGRE 14 caches the view space light position and direction arrays (AutoParamDataSource::mLightPosViewSpaceArray
  and mLightDirViewSpaceArray) and drops them only when the hash of the light list pointers changes
  (setCurrentLightList). The arrays depend on the view matrix as well, but a change of the camera or of the
  "identity view" state of the renderable (setCurrentCamera, setCurrentRenderable) does not drop them. When a
  renderable with an identity view (for example a full screen Rectangle2D) is drawn with the same light list as the
  following lit objects, it fills the arrays with the identity matrix and every following object with the same
  list reads world space light positions as view space positions: lights appear far from the object, so
  RTSS lit objects come out much darker than in OGRE 13.

  The fix drops both arrays (invalidateViewSpaceLights) when the identity view state or the camera changes and
  marks the light parameters dirty, so the next request recomputes them with the current view. It is the only
  change.

Affected OGRE file
  OgreMain/src/OgreAutoParamDataSource.cpp, setCurrentRenderable (identity view toggle, around line 116),
  setCurrentCamera (around line 155) and getLightPositionViewSpaceArray (around line 305), which fills the array
  only when it is smaller than the requested size.

Reproduction
  Draw a Rectangle2D with an identity view (the default for it) in the render queue before an Entity with an RTSS
  lit material, both getting the same light list (all nearby lights of a scene with 9 or fewer lights), then read
  light_position_view_space_array in the fragment program of the Entity: it holds the world positions of the
  lights instead of the view space positions. A lit object next to a point light is then lit far too weakly.

diff --git a/OgreMain/include/OgreAutoParamDataSource.h b/OgreMain/include/OgreAutoParamDataSource.h
index e529c83..9ee1bd2 100644
--- a/OgreMain/include/OgreAutoParamDataSource.h
+++ b/OgreMain/include/OgreAutoParamDataSource.h
@@ -156,6 +156,8 @@ namespace Ogre {
         /** Updates the current camera */
         void setCurrentCamera(const Camera* cam, bool useCameraRelative);
         void setCameraArray(const std::vector<const Camera*> cameras);
+        /// Drops the cached view space light positions and directions after the view changed
+        void invalidateViewSpaceLights();
         /** Sets the light list that should be used, and it's base index from the global list */
         void setCurrentLightList(const LightList* ll);
         /** Sets the current texture projector for a index */
diff --git a/OgreMain/src/OgreAutoParamDataSource.cpp b/OgreMain/src/OgreAutoParamDataSource.cpp
index ed34d1d..89ed67e 100644
--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreAutoParamDataSource.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreAutoParamDataSource.cpp
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@ namespace Ogre {
             mInverseViewMatrixDirty = true;
             mViewProjMatrixDirty = true;
             mGpuParamsDirty |= GPV_GLOBAL;
+            invalidateViewSpaceLights();
         }
 
         bool useIdentityProj = rend && rend->getUseIdentityProjection();
@@ -167,12 +168,21 @@ namespace Ogre {
         mCameraPositionDirty = true;
         mLodCameraPositionObjectSpaceDirty = true;
         mLodCameraPositionDirty = true;
+        invalidateViewSpaceLights();
     }
     void AutoParamDataSource::setCameraArray(const std::vector<const Camera*> cameras)
     {
         mCameraArray = cameras;
     }
     //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+    void AutoParamDataSource::invalidateViewSpaceLights()
+    {
+        // The view space light arrays are only dropped when the light list hash changes; they also depend on the view
+        mLightPosViewSpaceArray.clear();
+        mLightDirViewSpaceArray.clear();
+        mGpuParamsDirty |= GPV_LIGHTS;
+    }
+    //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     void AutoParamDataSource::setCurrentLightList(const LightList* ll)
     {
         static LightList NULL_LIGHTS;
